            "review_title": "Review at Yoshinoya Restaurant",
            "review_text": "Nicolas\n2 contributions\n0\nFROM A CUSTOMER TO A CUSTOMER – A CUSTOMER’S RELATIONSHIP\nApr 2026 • Friends\nI have supported Yoshinoya since the early days of the opening, but today’s experience is really a “shock” of the culture of service.\n• Translated attitude: I just walked into the restaurant for a moment when the staff standing on the counter shouted back in a loud voice, shaking like calling the worker: “Who are you going? You two sit there!” The resort was absent but still forced guests to sit at a small table at their own discretion with an ordering attitude. There were only two guests at the big table.\nThe uncultured welcome: When receiving orders, your staff lifted their faces and looked at the guests with a full attitude, absolutely not a silence. The highlight is that when you put the water out, you hit the \"bowl\" down the table like you want to screw the face of the guest for no reason.\n• Dealing with lies: I called a combo with salad and soup but it was missing. When questioned, the employee naturally argued the argument was \"combo is only that\". It was only when I pulled out the menu with my hands that you were silently filling up without an apology.\nIt’s really uncomprehensible for a large brand to re-train people who are so rude and lack respect for customers. If it doesn’t change, I’m sure the restaurant will soon eliminate itself from the market. One goes never back!\n\nI have been a frequent customer of Yoshinoya since its early days, but today’s experience was a total shock in terms of service culture.\nArrogant attitude: As I walked just a short distance into the restaurant, the counter staff shouted at me from behind, barking orders like I was a servant: \"How many people? If there are two, sit over there!\" Despite the restaurant being empty, they forced us into a tiny table with a commanding and rude tone.\nUnprofessional reception: During the ordering process, the staff threw their head up with a disrespectful look, without a single word of basic politeness. To make matters worse, they slammed my drink onto the table with a loud \"bang\" as if to intimidate me for no reason.\n• Dishonesty: I ordered a combo that clearly included salad and soup, but it was served incomplete. When I asked, the staff shamelessly argued that \"the combo only comes like this.\" Only after I pulled out the menu and pointed to the description did they silently bring out the missing items—without a single word of apology.\nIt’s hard to believe a major brand allows its staff to behave with such audacity and disrespect toward customers. I will never return. Management needs to take immediate action before losing all their loyal guests.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nTranslated from Vietnamese\nShow original\nWritten April 1, 2026",
